  "summary": "The prior critiques correctly identify the three unfiltered list_all() calls and the unconditional server-side replace at hub.go:354, but none pinpoints the actual flickering mechanism: the same TUI client sends two differently-shaped payloads to the same server field depending on which code path fires. The periodic push (tui.py:2093), auto-refresh (tui.py:2636), and auto-mode toggle (tui.py:2137) send unfiltered features (all boards), while board-filtered pushes at lines 2119 and 3330 send only the active board's features via _load_features(self.active_board). Because hub.go:354 does an unconditional replace (client.state.Features = features), the server oscillates between holding all-board data and single-board data for the same client. The webui polls /api/board which aggregates across clients — so when a filtered push lands between polls, the webui sees only active-board items; when the next periodic (unfiltered) push fires 0-5 seconds later, items reappear. This explains the reported symptom precisely: items load, then clear, then sometimes come back. The fourth critique's suggestion to fix the server's replace semantics is the right direction but overcomplicates it — the simplest correct fix is to make all push paths consistent by always sending unfiltered features. The two filtered call sites (lines 2119 and 3330) should use FeatureFile.list_all() instead of self._load_features(self.active_board), matching the pattern already used by the three other push sites. This preserves the aggregate view the /api/board endpoint is designed for, avoids any server-side merge complexity, and ensures the client never sends a partial snapshot that overwrites a complete one."
